// TEMPLATE — copy this file's output shape, don't hand-edit it directly.
//
// Real config.js is generated from your .env file by `node scripts/build-config.js`
// (see README → "Cross-device sync") and is gitignored, so your credentials never
// get committed. This file just documents what config.js looks like once built,
// so anyone cloning the repo understands the shape without needing to run the
// build script first.
//
// Note: a Supabase anon key is meant to be public — it's the same key your
// browser would send on every request either way. Row Level Security (not
// secrecy of this key) is what keeps each user's data private. Never put your
// Supabase service_role key here or anywhere client-side.

window.__SUPABASE_URL__ = "https://xxxxx.supabase.co";
window.__SUPABASE_ANON_KEY__ = "eyJhbGciOi...";